lesson('concurrency', [
 ('One', [['title','One after another'],['code','water("peas")    # 2 seconds'],['code','water("kale")    # 2 seconds'],['code','water("leeks")   # 2 seconds'],['out','→ 6 seconds']],
  "Four beds need watering, and each sprinkler takes two seconds. Water peas, then kale, then leeks, one after another, and you wait six seconds.",
  ['Four beds need watering','Water peas','then kale','then leeks','you wait six seconds']),
 ('Waiting', [['title','Waiting is wasted'],['code','time.sleep(2)'],['chalk','the computer does nothing'],['chalk','while it waits for the water']],
  "Most of that time, the computer is just waiting. time dot sleep, two. It does nothing while the water runs. Concurrency means doing other jobs while you wait.",
  ['Most of that time','time dot sleep, two','It does nothing','Concurrency means']),
 ('Threads', [['title','Threads'],['code','import threading'],['code','t = threading.Thread(target=water, args=("peas",))'],['code','t.start(); t.join()']],
  "One way is threads. import threading. t equals threading dot Thread, target water, args peas. t dot start starts it, and t dot join waits for it to finish.",
  ['One way is threads','import threading','t equals threading dot Thread','t dot start starts it']),
 ('Processes', [['title','Processes for heavy maths'],['code','from multiprocessing import Pool'],['code','with Pool() as pool:'],['code','    pool.map(count_seeds, trays)']],
  "Threads are good for waiting. For heavy maths, use processes, which really run on several cores. from multiprocessing import Pool. with Pool as pool: pool dot map, count seeds, over all the trays.",
  ['Threads are good for waiting','from multiprocessing import Pool','with Pool as pool','pool dot map']),
 ('async', [['title','async and await'],['code','async def water(bed):'],['code','    await asyncio.sleep(2)'],['code','    print(bed, "done")']],
  "The modern way to wait is async. async def water, bed. await asyncio dot sleep, two. While it waits, other jobs can run. Then print bed, done.",
  ['The modern way to wait is async','async def water','await asyncio dot sleep','Then print bed, done']),
 ('gather', [['title','Run many: gather'],['code','async def main():'],['code','    await asyncio.gather(water("peas"), water("kale"))'],['code','asyncio.run(main())'],['out','→ about 2 seconds, not 4']],
  "To run many at once, use gather. async def main. await asyncio dot gather, water peas, water kale. asyncio dot run, main. Both sprinklers wait together, so it takes about two seconds, not four.",
  ['To run many at once','async def main','await asyncio dot gather','asyncio dot run','about two seconds']),
 ('Safe', [['title','Sharing safely'],['code','lock = threading.Lock()'],['code','with lock:'],['code','    tank -= 5']],
  "When threads share something, take turns. lock equals threading dot Lock. with lock: tank minus equals five. Only one thread can change the tank at a time.",
  ['When threads share something','lock equals threading dot Lock','with lock','Only one thread']),
 ('Choose', [['title','Which to choose'],['chalk','waiting (files, internet) → async or threads'],['chalk','heavy maths → processes'],['chalk','small jobs → keep it simple']],
  "Which to choose? Waiting for files or the internet: async or threads. Heavy maths: processes. For small jobs, keep it simple and do one thing at a time.",
  ['Which to choose','Waiting for files or the internet','Heavy maths: processes','For small jobs']),
])
